  "body": "## What changed\n- `.github/workflows/cut.yml`: both jobs move from `runs-on: [self-hosted, linux]` to `runs-on: [self-hosted, camcraft-cut]`.\n- AGENTS.md and `.claude/skills/runners/SKILL.md` now say the cut runner carries `camcraft-cut`, and that only the cut runner carries it.\n- `docs/decisions/3253-cut-runner-label.md` records the choice.\n\nWhy: GitHub matches labels case-insensitively. All eight post-merge runners (`self-hosted,Linux,X64,camcraft-post-merge`) therefore matched `[self-hosted, linux]`, so a 5-hour release gate could land on an 8-thread or 24 GB machine.\n\n## ⚠️ Merge order: not during a cut, and only after the label exists\n1. Settings -> Actions -> Runners -> **wopr** -> add the label **`camcraft-cut`**. Optionally add it to `uma` too, as a backup. No re-registration is needed.\n2. Then merge this.\n\nIf `cut.yml` asks for `camcraft-cut` before any runner has it, the gate waits in the queue forever. For tonight's cut, a stop-gap on the runner owner's side keeps the gate on `wopr`: every other runner is stopped while the release PR is open.\n\n## How tested\n- Read only. A workflow label change can't be exercised without a cut.\n- `git grep` shows no other file names `cut.yml`'s labels. `RECOMMENDED.md` holds historical records, which stay as written.\n\n## Process files\nProcess change: yes\nAGENTS.md and `.claude/skills/runners/SKILL.md` change, so the merging session bumps `PROCESS_VERSION` and posts the note on #681.\n\nChangelog: none (CI and process only)\n\nFixes #3253\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
